---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Kvisl" description="How Kvisl collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information.">
  <main class="container page-main narrow-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated 19 September 2026</p>

    <div class="policy-copy">
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> handles personal information when you visit the site, subscribe, contact us, request a licence, donate, or otherwise use our services. We aim to collect only what is reasonably necessary for those purposes.</p>

      <div class="policy-contact-box">
        <strong>Privacy contact</strong>
        <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Information you provide</h2>
      <p>We may receive information you choose to provide, including your name, email address, organisation or publication, correspondence, licensing details, donation-related messages, and anything else you include in a form or email.</p>
      <p>If you subscribe, we store your email address so we can send new essays and occasional editorial notes. If you request republication, we may retain the details needed to review the request, prepare terms, administer the licence, and keep an appropriate record.</p>

      <h2>2. Technical information</h2>
      <p>When you use the site, our hosting, security, database, delivery, and infrastructure providers may process routine technical data such as your IP address, browser and device type, operating system, request time, referring page, requested URL, and diagnostic or security logs.</p>
      <p>We use this data to deliver the site, maintain reliability, diagnose faults, prevent abuse, protect the service, and understand basic operational performance. We do not use it to build behavioural advertising profiles.</p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p>The site may use essential cookies or local browser storage for functions such as remembering your appearance preference, maintaining security, or preserving a necessary session. We do not use those settings for targeted advertising.</p>

      <h2>4. How we use personal information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to deliver subscriptions and other requested communications;</li>
        <li>to respond to editorial, rights, privacy, correction, and general enquiries;</li>
        <li>to review and administer republication and licensing requests;</li>
        <li>to operate, secure, maintain, and improve the site;</li>
        <li>to detect and prevent fraud, misuse, and technical abuse;</li>
        <li>to keep records needed for contracts, licensing, accounting, disputes, or legal obligations;</li>
        <li>to comply with applicable law and protect our rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Basis for processing</h2>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances and applicable law, we process personal information because you have asked us to provide a service, because it is necessary to administer a request or agreement, because we have a legitimate operational or security interest, because you have consented, or because we must comply with a legal obligation.</p>

      <h2>6. Service providers</h2>
      <p>We may use third-party providers for hosting, databases, email delivery, security, and other technical functions. They may process limited information on our behalf only as needed to provide those services.</p>
      <p>We do not sell personal information or subscriber lists to advertisers, data brokers, or unrelated third parties.</p>

      <h2>7. International processing</h2>
      <p>Some service providers may operate in more than one country, so information may be processed outside the country where you live. Where required, we take reasonable steps to use appropriate service providers and contractual protections.</p>

      <h2>8. Retention</h2>
      <p>We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, including service delivery, security, record-keeping, licensing, dispute resolution, and legal or accounting requirements.</p>
      <p>After you unsubscribe, we may retain a limited suppression record so we can honour your request not to receive future subscription messages.</p>

      <h2>9. Your choices and requests</h2>
      <p>You can unsubscribe through the link included in our emails. Where applicable, you may also ask to access, correct, delete, or restrict the use of personal information we hold about you.</p>
      <p>We may need to verify your identity before completing a request. Certain records may still need to be kept where required by law or reasonably necessary for security, transactions, record-keeping, or legal claims.</p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards designed to protect personal information from unauthorised access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure. No internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
      <p>Do not send passwords, wallet private keys, seed phrases, authentication codes, or similarly sensitive credentials to <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>.</p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p><span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> is a general-audience publication and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly seek personal information from children through the site.</p>

      <h2>12. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>Articles may link to external websites. Those sites are governed by their own privacy practices and policies.</p>

      <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may revise this policy as our services, technology, or legal obligations change. The date above will be updated whenever a material revision is published.</p>

      <h2>14. Contact</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
